WEBVTT

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:11.920
What still sounds like a fairy tale today can be reality tomorrow.

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:14.040
Here is a fairy tale of the day after tomorrow.

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:16.210
There are no more national states.

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:19.680
There is only humanity and its colonies in space.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:22.830
You settle on distant stars.

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:25.930
The seabed is closed as a living space.

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:29.970
With still unimaginable speeds today, through a space...

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:39.640
One of these spaceships is the Orion, a tiny part of a gigantic security system that protects the Earth from threats from space.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:45.110
We accompany the Orion and its crew on their patrol service on the brink of infinity.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:24.260
EAS4 calls Orion. Orion 7, call in. Call in and give your coordinates.

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:08.930
Out of order. Your Alpha order...

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:11.570
Out of order to Orion 7.

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:14.780
Instant return to Space Station 13.

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:16.780
Orion, do you hear me?

00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:20.020
The highest space authority gives Alpha order.

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:21.630
Instant return.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.320
On command. Resonance contact.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:37.210
This is the Orion 7, under Commander Cliff Alastair McLane.

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:41.280
To the highest space authority, Section 12, Department of Astro-Technics,

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:42.900
over Jupiter Outer and EAS 3.

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:47.900
To harden my claim that a landing on Rhea is possible,

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:50.040
I will set up on Rhea in a few moments.

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:54.960
That was the Orion. I'll switch off now.

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:57.120
Get ready for landing.

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:01.580
the driver went to the hospital

00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:49.350
I'll let you pray.

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:58.000
General Van Dyck, you probably know why I asked you to come here.

00:03:58.500 --> 00:03:59.820
You think so?

00:04:01.150 --> 00:04:02.010
McLean, am I right?

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:03.600
Yes, General, it is time.

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:06.600
The unscrupulous landing on Rhea broke his neck.

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:09.600
The landing on Rhea may have been unscrupulous,

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:11.960
but it was a space-traveling masterpiece.

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:15.720
It was carried out against an explicit alpha order of the highest authority.

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:21.420
That you, Commander McLean, would prefer to see criminals in the phosphor swamps is nothing new to me.

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:24.880
No, as for the matter, General, personal sympathies or antipathies do not matter here.

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:29.560
The fact is that McLean, with immediate effect on the patrol service of space,

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.660
that the intelligence association is guilty of a crime.

00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:37.450
Nobody came to inform me as McLean's former supervisor.

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:40.390
That's why I asked you to come here.

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:42.290
McLean and his crew will arrive here in a few minutes.

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:45.220
Aha. So I'm supposed to live in the direction?

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:47.560
I would have liked to have spared you.

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:48.860
You know what, General?

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:52.960
I consider this crime to be the biggest scandal in the entire space fleet.

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:55.320
So? And McLean's escapades?

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:56.900
His constant Hussar knights on their own?

00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:57.900
Wasn't that a scandal?

00:04:58.140 --> 00:04:59.640
The crazy flight to the second Jupiter moon?

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:06.080
The breakthrough to the Saturn base in the Second Stellar War, the self-propelled intervention on Alpha Centauri and so on and so forth were not scandals.

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:08.260
Without men like MacLean we would have probably lost the two Stellar Wars.

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:13.880
Really? But curse again, we are not gathered on MacLean.

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:18.180
MacLean and patrol service general. It would have been better if he had been thrown out right away.

00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:22.190
Let's not dramatize it, General. No man is irreplaceable.

00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:24.330
In a few years we will only have robots sitting in our spacesuit.

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:27.560
Hopefully also in the front rooms of the headquarters.

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:28.550
General?

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:31.700
The crew of the Orion is here.

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:33.280
Get in with it.

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:36.680
General, shouldn't we first go to the security service officer?

00:05:36.820 --> 00:05:41.270
Yes, this lady first.

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:42.360
Yes, General.

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:43.700
Please, Lieutenant.

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:47.000
Does that mean that McLean will also get a sniffer on board?

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:49.120
Order of the upper room authority.

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:50.140
I can't change it.

00:05:58.640 --> 00:05:59.920
Lieutenant Tamara Jagalowska.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.340
from the Galactic Security Service.

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:03.880
This is General Van Dyck,

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:05.060
head of the rapid space associations

00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:06.900
that the Orion crew has been subjugating so far.

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:10.080
You know the reports, the files, documents

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:12.220
and individual disciplinary procedures

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:13.600
about the Orion team, Lieutenant?

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:14.520
Yes, General.

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:15.600
You know your tasks

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:17.160
and know about your service on the Orion?

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:18.850
I was informed about this

00:06:18.850 --> 00:06:20.070
in the headquarters of the Security Service.

00:06:21.050 --> 00:06:22.430
As a security officer,

00:06:22.470 --> 00:06:23.090
you are commissioned on the Orion

00:06:23.090 --> 00:06:24.910
to command transgressions,

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:27.440
violations against the space service regulations

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:29.090
and violations of fleet laws

00:06:29.090 --> 00:06:29.810
in a disciplinary manner.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:32.160
or to report it.

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:33.580
That is my order.

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:36.380
You will not have it easy with McLane and his people.

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:37.430
I expect so.

00:06:37.610 --> 00:06:41.550
You are still quite young for such a task.

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:45.080
And you do not have much experience in the galactic service.

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:46.940
They beat me up, General.

00:06:49.670 --> 00:06:50.970
Well, then it can start.

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:53.240
Come in with McLane and his gang.

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:55.840
Yes, General. Commander, please.

00:07:00.510 --> 00:07:13.240
... McLean and the Orion crew.

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:18.300
Major, the Inspection Committee of the Interplanetary Space Commission has ordered.

00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:23.100
Your service-supply relationship to the rapid space associations will be lifted immediately.

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:25.400
You have been considered to be a penalty for the space patrol service.

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:29.970
For how long...

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.730
For three years.

00:07:33.460 --> 00:07:35.440
And why?

00:07:36.270 --> 00:07:40.430
Major McLean, spare yourself and give me the list of your special events.

00:07:41.050 --> 00:07:44.190
In the future, Major, you will get your farewell at the least against the regulations.

00:07:45.090 --> 00:07:47.970
Are we in agreement on this, commander?

00:07:48.940 --> 00:07:54.950
General, if the defense staff wishes so, I will still withdraw the consequences from the space fleet service today.

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:57.520
You are now keeping your mouth shut, McLean.

00:07:57.560 --> 00:07:59.570
You will not quit the service either.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:03.600
You are not an insulted cadet, but you will return to me in three years.

00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:04.800
Understood?

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:07.260
Yes, General.

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:08.740
General?

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:16.270
There would be something else.

00:08:16.450 --> 00:08:25.030
There is a remote order from the command staff that a member of the Galactic Security Service

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:26.090
be set aside for this time.

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:27.920
General, this can not be.

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:28.880
No comment if I may ask.

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:34.660
This is your future security officer, Lieutenant Tamara Jagalovs.

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:39.320
I'm sure McLean knows that the GSD officers can carry out the Alpha Order.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:44.820
I hope there's no trouble, McLean.

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:48.420
I hope so, General.

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:55.250
Good. Then I'd like to talk to you and your crew about your first mission in the Space Patrol.

00:08:56.110 --> 00:08:59.360
You'll take off tomorrow at 6 p.m. from Deep Sea Base 104.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.840
to Space Sector 219-33-9.

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:06.600
Your task, Commander, is to monitor, secure and control

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:09.300
all space ships and long-range satellite movements in this sector.

00:09:09.780 --> 00:09:12.780
General, that's an order for space cadets, isn't it?

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:14.700
Consider it a rest trip.

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:16.960
You look like you've been attacked anyway.

00:09:17.380 --> 00:09:18.190
Is that clear?

00:09:18.530 --> 00:09:21.280
All right, General.

00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:24.200
Then my adjutant Spring-Brauner will inform you

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:25.160
about the situation in this sector.

00:09:26.360 --> 00:09:29.980
Space Sector 219-33-9.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.920
The new McLean, the neighboring sectors, don't care about them.

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:34.190
Do we understand?

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:36.220
Yes, General.

00:09:36.420 --> 00:09:38.360
Thank you.

00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:43.910
May I ask for your esteemed attention?

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:45.570
You may...

00:09:45.570 --> 00:09:46.190
No, Hasso.

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:47.820
Not him.

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:20.880
No, not for me, I have to go now.

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:23.800
Really Cliff, I should already be at home for two hours.

00:10:24.200 --> 00:10:24.880
Yes, then go.

00:10:25.160 --> 00:10:29.360
Yes, I really have to get on my way.

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:32.470
What did you ask me?

00:10:33.210 --> 00:10:34.340
I asked you?

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:36.600
Yes, you just asked me something.

00:10:37.210 --> 00:10:39.230
Right, I asked you if you want a cognac.

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:43.790
Yes, I do. But then I have to go.

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:45.490
Otherwise Ingrid will get angry.

00:10:45.730 --> 00:10:46.270
Yes, you're right.

00:10:49.060 --> 00:10:50.160
Don't you want to come with me?

00:10:51.560 --> 00:10:54.040
Dear time, is it time again?

00:10:55.610 --> 00:10:57.190
Yes, I promised her.

00:10:58.150 --> 00:10:59.200
How often did you promise her?

00:11:00.410 --> 00:11:01.210
Tell me, do you keep thinking about that?

00:11:02.770 --> 00:11:03.970
That's my serious, Cliff.

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:05.480
Stop it.

00:11:05.880 --> 00:11:08.100
Is that your serious, or was that your serious?

00:11:09.860 --> 00:11:10.300
Sorry.

00:11:13.120 --> 00:11:16.120
You have to talk to her.

00:11:16.520 --> 00:11:17.340
Yes, I know.

00:11:17.720 --> 00:11:20.080
Without you, I wouldn't dare to go home.

00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:22.480
That's not necessary anymore.

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:24.520
I'm sorry.

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:25.960
It happened.

00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:27.350
The numbers?

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:29.290
You're going to get me into trouble now.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.220
No, no, just numbers. It's better when we've already paid.

00:11:32.660 --> 00:11:33.200
That's good.

00:11:35.480 --> 00:11:38.780
Honey, hello. I was just at the...

00:11:38.780 --> 00:11:39.300
Hello, Major.

00:11:39.460 --> 00:11:42.770
So, are all the team meetings taking place here?

00:11:43.250 --> 00:11:45.650
Some of them, yes. That's fantastic.

00:11:45.710 --> 00:11:46.930
I have the impression, too.

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:49.680
As I said, we were just at the...

00:11:49.680 --> 00:11:52.300
I suggested to Cliff that he should come with us for a beer.

00:11:52.740 --> 00:11:52.940
What?

00:11:54.410 --> 00:11:57.250
Ingrid, you don't seem to be very enthusiastic about the team...

00:11:57.250 --> 00:11:59.970
I see. Every time you drag your chat to us, I know exactly what...

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.040
Yes, Ingrid, I thought...

00:12:05.600 --> 00:12:07.430
How should I explain this?

00:12:07.430 --> 00:12:08.770
You don't need to explain anything to me, Major.

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:10.640
Hasso is going with us again.

00:12:10.760 --> 00:12:11.040
Yes.

00:12:11.200 --> 00:12:12.480
That's right, Ingrid.

00:12:13.490 --> 00:12:15.370
I thought it would be better if I was there this time.

00:12:16.070 --> 00:12:17.530
This one time...

00:12:17.530 --> 00:12:19.070
Yes, especially now that we are so popular in higher places.

00:12:19.930 --> 00:12:23.480
They even ordered a guard from the GSD to come to us.

00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:26.360
It would be unprofitable at this time to have a successor for Hasso.

00:12:26.440 --> 00:12:26.560
Exactly.

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:29.000
I'm excited to hear your excuses.

00:12:30.800 --> 00:12:32.540
Cliff, she laughed.

00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:34.160
Let's just say she smiled.

00:12:35.700 --> 00:12:36.640
Let's drink to that.

00:13:01.120 --> 00:13:03.420
The base will be free in a few minutes.

00:13:04.040 --> 00:13:06.200
Stay in landing position until you are called off.

00:13:06.520 --> 00:13:10.040
I'm warning you that we're coming from Andromeda 17 Beta 12.

00:13:10.380 --> 00:13:12.080
Do you understand? That's enough for us.

00:13:12.120 --> 00:13:13.300
We've been in the room for 18 weeks.

00:13:14.190 --> 00:13:17.190
I'm sorry, Commander. The base has been blocked by the Orion 7.

00:13:18.170 --> 00:13:21.070
McClane? I think he's with the Fast Space Associations.

00:13:21.170 --> 00:13:22.820
What is he doing on Base 104?

00:13:23.340 --> 00:13:26.440
You can ask him when you meet him next time in the Starlight Casino.

00:13:26.940 --> 00:13:29.720
Ha ha ha! Please connect me to Colonel Mulligan.

00:13:30.090 --> 00:13:31.590
I demand that we be transferred to a different base.

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:36.340
The bases 81 to 106 are occupied by the 2nd Galactic Fleet.

00:13:36.900 --> 00:13:39.160
I'm sorry. Besides, the Commander is on vacation.

00:13:39.490 --> 00:13:41.090
On vacation? That's probably...

00:13:41.090 --> 00:13:43.430
Commander Stein, you've been in the room for 18 weeks.

00:13:44.110 --> 00:13:47.990
Do you want to risk a disciplinary procedure just because you have to wait five minutes now?

00:13:48.350 --> 00:13:50.800
We're still breaking up, darling.

00:13:51.420 --> 00:13:55.230
You're welcome, Commander. Just ask yourself what your wife says about it.

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:09.340
Is the computer checked? Is the course programed?

00:14:09.340 --> 00:14:13.960
Yes, the Schlaumeier is in order, but don't ask me what kind of enchanting bug I had to replace for it.

00:14:13.980 --> 00:14:14.520
No one asks that.

00:14:14.960 --> 00:14:16.020
She was from a...

00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:17.620
Board control, Lieutenant Montse.

00:14:17.820 --> 00:14:19.680
Board control?

00:14:20.890 --> 00:14:24.470
Lieutenant Tamara Jagalowsk from the Galactic Security Service is reporting on board.

00:14:24.790 --> 00:14:26.470
Control center running, Commander.

00:14:31.020 --> 00:14:33.740
Commandant to Astrogator, control to automatic.

00:14:35.750 --> 00:14:38.470
Automatic control at CD minus 10, boss.

00:14:39.300 --> 00:14:43.940
Space surveillance running, light beam is on. Orion ground base in contact with Earth's outer station 4.

00:14:44.620 --> 00:14:50.680
Base 104, start control on the fast space cruiser Orion 7. You are free to go.

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:52.000
Thank you, base.

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:55.900
Base 104, continue to transfer to Earth's outer station 4.

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:58.100
Ready to go, first acceleration.

00:14:58.940 --> 00:14:59.980
Commander McLean, may I...

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:05.760
Lieutenant Jagielowsk, I don't need any help or surveillance for the start, so please go to your cabin.

00:15:05.940 --> 00:15:10.420
Turn on the voice connection, that's a small button, on which it says BSA, on-board speaker system.

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:13.650
If you don't want to be seen, you have the visiophone at your disposal.

00:15:13.850 --> 00:15:20.900
In the built-in closet you'll find your on-board luggage, including a nursing set for 12 months and a paralyser pistol, if you want to paralyse yourself.

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:25.560
But if you don't want to be seen, you still have our cold sleeping chamber at your disposal.

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:27.740
You want to freeze me too much, don't you, Commander?

00:15:28.220 --> 00:15:29.870
What I want is unfortunately not available.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:35.390
Go to your cabin. If something happens to you, it means I've committed a murder attack on you.

00:15:35.790 --> 00:15:42.730
G is 1, approach 05.

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:44.580
You stay up, Hasse.

00:15:44.740 --> 00:15:46.480
I'm on autopilot and control.

00:15:46.940 --> 00:15:47.480
Let's go again.

00:16:00.030 --> 00:16:00.710
Thank you.

00:16:32.200 --> 00:16:58.370
The Polish in tongues of the law.

00:16:58.470 --> 00:16:59.970
The government was not the

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:01.120
We're going to stay in your cabin for the rest of the night.

00:17:01.120 --> 00:17:04.190
Do you want us to stay in your cabin for the rest of the night?

00:17:04.630 --> 00:17:05.790
That's not going to happen.

00:17:06.360 --> 00:17:07.680
We're going to finish this snitch already.

00:17:08.420 --> 00:17:09.020
Leave her alone.

00:17:09.180 --> 00:17:09.940
Or you and me.

00:17:10.040 --> 00:17:11.860
I have a feeling she won't like eating cherries.

00:17:12.340 --> 00:17:13.280
Eating cherries?

00:17:13.620 --> 00:17:15.560
Isn't that exactly what I'm going to do with her?

00:17:16.120 --> 00:17:17.340
Oh, old gambler.

00:17:17.440 --> 00:17:19.980
Just don't pretend that you only have the slightest chance with her.

00:17:20.220 --> 00:17:21.400
But Helga, no.

00:17:21.840 --> 00:17:23.280
Who's going to be jealous now?

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:23.920
Me?

00:17:25.560 --> 00:17:27.200
A dispute about the emperor's beard.

00:17:27.420 --> 00:17:29.420
In my eyes, that's one as a girl...

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:31.400
She's a robot. But not a woman.

00:17:32.420 --> 00:17:35.500
We'll see. Let's see what she does.

00:17:42.400 --> 00:17:43.180
Looks like she's changed.

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:47.270
Ah, she's in good shape too.

00:17:48.370 --> 00:17:50.210
Do you think I can ask her to clean up my cabin?

00:17:51.090 --> 00:17:52.590
Are you crazy? We don't have that.

00:17:53.090 --> 00:17:56.820
If you see or talk to her, tell her you don't like BSA as it should be.

00:17:56.820 --> 00:17:59.300
I'm sorry Cliff, she was completely dressed up.

00:18:01.950 --> 00:18:07.360
Lieutenant De Monte to Security Officer Jagielowski.

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:09.860
Are you ready to speak? Then please switch on your microphone.

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:11.490
Excuse me?

00:18:11.630 --> 00:18:15.420
Please tell me an extraordinary question.

00:18:15.720 --> 00:18:19.040
Would you like a sip of whiskey in my cabin?

00:18:19.360 --> 00:18:20.870
Do you have the whiskey?

00:18:21.420 --> 00:18:23.520
Yes, of course, my dearest. A whole box.

00:18:24.820 --> 00:18:26.920
That's very interesting. Thank you for the information.

00:18:27.430 --> 00:18:29.050
Unfortunately, I have to make a report about it.

00:18:33.760 --> 00:18:38.040
Astrogator and commander, an alpha message from the solar weather station Dragom.

00:18:38.080 --> 00:18:39.340
I'm going over amplifiers.

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:45.500
In sector 207, 24, 8, eruptive weather has arisen,

00:18:45.500 --> 00:18:49.000
which is moving at a speed of 38 to 52.

00:18:49.700 --> 00:18:51.980
To sector 229.

00:18:53.590 --> 00:18:57.010
The eruptions have a duration of 27 minutes.

00:18:57.390 --> 00:18:59.590
The radiation reaches about 150 degrees.

00:19:01.060 --> 00:19:03.760
Automatics off. Machines occupied. We're going to the escape coordinates.

00:19:04.100 --> 00:19:08.860
Other coordinates? Then I'll immediately try to teach you our course change at Earth Station 4, Commander.

00:19:08.860 --> 00:19:11.120
There's no way to do that with such a solar storm.

00:19:11.320 --> 00:19:12.420
Space monitoring, shielding.

00:19:12.840 --> 00:19:16.140
The EAS-4 is a total mess for the ghosts, and do you think they could help us?

00:19:16.280 --> 00:19:19.600
Solar eruptions generate radiation up to ten thousand times more than normal.

00:19:19.900 --> 00:19:21.880
I'll try to teach you the EAS-4, Commander.

00:19:22.060 --> 00:19:23.360
Stay away from me, lieutenant.

00:19:23.460 --> 00:19:26.940
If a solar storm breaks the entire radio traffic, should I send it a warning card?

00:19:53.450 --> 00:19:56.200
You can always do it!

00:20:00.280 --> 00:20:04.760
If the intensity of the radiation is 10,000 times the intensity of the normal radiation in space,

00:20:05.280 --> 00:20:08.360
why then doesn't the Orion need 10,000 times the radiation?

00:20:08.780 --> 00:20:11.880
The radiation is, of course, based on the strongest possible radiation.

00:20:13.040 --> 00:20:14.600
The cascade principle is used to do that.

00:20:14.600 --> 00:20:17.100
Who cares? That's why you can't keep a beginner's lesson anywhere else.

00:20:17.640 --> 00:20:19.460
Well, what are you talking about?

00:20:22.560 --> 00:20:23.600
264 has worms.

00:20:24.110 --> 00:20:25.130
Oh, the poor thing.

00:20:25.720 --> 00:20:26.440
Doesn't eat anymore.

00:20:26.840 --> 00:20:27.040
No.

00:20:27.540 --> 00:20:28.520
And I'm not with him.

00:20:28.760 --> 00:20:29.860
But he's really shy.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:31.800
Please, who's 264?

00:20:32.100 --> 00:20:35.750
His dog, a poodle. One of the last 376 poodles there are.

00:20:36.170 --> 00:20:36.890
You're worried.

00:20:37.350 --> 00:20:40.300
We're juggling past a solar storm and you're only thinking about...

00:20:43.020 --> 00:20:43.820
Exploding!

00:20:47.160 --> 00:20:49.770
Hm, yes. That's what space travelers always have to do.

00:20:50.820 --> 00:20:52.180
Commander, something has to happen.

00:20:52.460 --> 00:20:53.240
Yes, something will happen.

00:20:53.880 --> 00:20:54.680
And what are you thinking of doing?

00:20:55.140 --> 00:20:56.730
I'm going to eat something.

00:20:57.690 --> 00:20:58.950
That's a brilliant idea.

00:20:59.270 --> 00:20:59.970
Take me to...

00:21:00.030 --> 00:21:01.930
Of course, onion soup or pepper steak.

00:21:02.150 --> 00:21:03.860
Yes, yes, I think he'll be fine.

00:21:03.980 --> 00:21:05.210
Bon appetit!

00:21:05.250 --> 00:21:14.980
What does the cascade principle mean?

00:21:15.040 --> 00:21:16.200
I tried to explain it to him.

00:21:16.220 --> 00:21:18.580
You think you can sell me for a fool, don't you?

00:21:18.620 --> 00:21:19.440
But I beg you.

00:21:19.460 --> 00:21:22.300
Major McLean was just looking for a reason and a way to end the race.

00:21:22.900 --> 00:21:29.980
But you're a little short on the...

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:33.120
The radiation storm has passed us. It's shaking us quite a bit, doesn't it have to be?

00:21:33.300 --> 00:21:36.180
The officer of the GSD doesn't like it when we change the course.

00:21:36.850 --> 00:21:38.110
So I changed it as little as possible.

00:21:38.750 --> 00:21:40.200
And now it's rustling a bit.

00:21:40.900 --> 00:21:41.800
Oh, I understand.

00:21:42.360 --> 00:21:43.540
Hopefully they understand it too.

00:21:43.820 --> 00:21:45.900
And you think you'll get her on this tour, yes?

00:21:46.380 --> 00:21:47.360
That's good what you can do.

00:21:48.420 --> 00:21:58.780
Yes, I'll eat her.

00:22:00.440 --> 00:22:01.420
A cobra is also pretty.

00:22:02.600 --> 00:22:09.490
One thing is for sure, she doesn't do a three-year security service with us.

00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:14.230
Either she's insane after the first three operations, or...

00:22:14.230 --> 00:22:14.450
Or?

00:22:14.710 --> 00:22:16.070
She's a commander.

00:22:16.450 --> 00:22:29.350
Order 33.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:34.670
Five, thirty, twenty-nine, twenty-six are passing.

00:22:34.670 --> 00:22:36.130
Do you get any radio contact, Arthur?

00:22:37.140 --> 00:22:37.520
Nothing.

00:22:38.670 --> 00:22:39.770
There's something in the tower outside.

00:22:39.910 --> 00:22:42.900
It's a disturbed radio satellite. Type Sky 77.

00:22:43.380 --> 00:22:44.760
Probably Terracosmos control.

00:22:45.240 --> 00:22:46.000
It must have been hit by the eruption.

00:22:47.220 --> 00:22:48.640
In any case, the thing is dead.

00:22:48.920 --> 00:22:49.700
Come on, Mario, shoot it.

00:22:49.940 --> 00:22:50.640
All right, Cliff.

00:22:50.920 --> 00:22:54.010
Are you able to eliminate a radio satellite that easily?

00:22:54.870 --> 00:22:56.880
My dear child.

00:22:57.160 --> 00:22:58.520
I'm not your dear child.

00:22:58.780 --> 00:22:59.840
I'm the responsible one.

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:04.340
I'm a GSD officer on board and I forbid you to shoot the satellites, as you like to express yourself.

00:23:04.760 --> 00:23:07.870
This body out there has a value of 12,000 credits.

00:23:08.330 --> 00:23:11.150
This body, as you say so nicely, has no value at all.

00:23:11.190 --> 00:23:15.500
It poses a threat to the entire space ship crew within three sectors.

00:23:16.600 --> 00:23:22.420
Don't you believe that there is a space station or an E-station that has already determined that the satellite is no longer working?

00:23:22.860 --> 00:23:28.440
Not even I know how many satellites, measuring probes and radar machines are hovering around here, probably 25,000.

00:23:28.740 --> 00:23:29.760
In addition to that, we have a pretty little...

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:36.120
I warn you, Commander, there's probably already a Techno-Hilfs-Kreuzer on the way to investigate the matter.

00:23:36.740 --> 00:23:38.240
You're not eliminating the satellite.

00:23:39.020 --> 00:23:47.880
Lieutenant De Monti, speak on board.

00:23:48.160 --> 00:23:54.490
The GSD officer Tamara Jagielowsk forbids the ejection of the radio satellite on the coordinates sowieso sowieso and so on and so on.

00:23:54.670 --> 00:23:56.520
The Commander goes to sleep.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:03.060
I'm afraid the commander won't go to bed. We're just passing by MZ-4.

00:24:03.240 --> 00:24:03.540
So?

00:24:05.400 --> 00:24:06.220
Clarence won't call.

00:24:06.300 --> 00:24:14.180
What? MZ-4 won't call?

00:24:14.220 --> 00:24:15.960
I've never been there.

00:24:15.980 --> 00:24:16.660
Try again.

00:24:17.000 --> 00:24:19.240
What is MZ-4?

00:24:19.480 --> 00:24:23.420
A relay and remote station that was set up a few years ago.

00:24:23.760 --> 00:24:25.820
And who is Clarence?

00:24:26.000 --> 00:24:28.480
Head of the station and a friend of ours.

00:24:28.600 --> 00:24:29.980
And if he doesn't call, it's either...

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:30.720
Either dead or drunk.

00:24:32.240 --> 00:24:32.880
So, what is it?

00:24:33.230 --> 00:24:33.550
Nothing.

00:24:34.690 --> 00:24:37.240
Orion 7 calling MZ-4.

00:24:37.520 --> 00:24:38.320
Clarence, please report.

00:24:38.560 --> 00:24:40.250
We just want to say good day.

00:24:44.900 --> 00:24:45.540
Well, well.

00:24:47.110 --> 00:24:48.450
These are three groups I've never heard of in my life.

00:24:49.210 --> 00:24:51.440
Should I stop them?

00:24:51.480 --> 00:24:52.600
Yes, I want to know what's going on.

00:24:52.760 --> 00:24:55.980
Commander, you have instructions to reach your area of operation as soon as possible.

00:24:56.420 --> 00:24:58.340
Listen to this. MZ-4 is crazy.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:01.220
What a crazy, senseless code.

00:25:01.500 --> 00:25:05.800
Is it important for your mission to know whether MZ-4 is lying or not?

00:25:06.600 --> 00:25:09.590
If you were one of us, Lieutenant, I would tell you now,

00:25:10.230 --> 00:25:12.930
we don't care what's going on with our friend Clarence.

00:25:13.350 --> 00:25:19.010
But since you are a security officer, I have another answer for you.

00:25:19.220 --> 00:25:23.620
In about 48 hours, the automatic lab cruiser Challenger will pass the MZ-4.

00:25:24.240 --> 00:25:26.850
It is to get its new course correction from there.

00:25:27.540 --> 00:25:29.600
But if it gets this instead, there will be a catastrophe.

00:25:30.480 --> 00:25:32.890
Then the cruiser will rush against the meteorite, of course.

00:25:33.050 --> 00:25:40.550
It lights up, but don't you have the possibility of feeding the Challenger's electron brain with a radio correction?

00:25:41.330 --> 00:25:46.610
I would have had this possibility if you hadn't forbidden me to kill the dead satellite.

00:25:48.160 --> 00:25:51.300
This little deaf taste that was so dear to you

00:25:51.300 --> 00:25:54.280
is exactly disturbed by the frequencies that lie on the Challenger's coordinates.

00:25:54.480 --> 00:25:55.360
So what happens?

00:25:56.760 --> 00:25:58.700
Landing on MZ-4. Try to maintain the disturbance.

00:26:00.220 --> 00:26:03.560
Do you know what a self-reliant course change has to mean in your life?

00:26:03.700 --> 00:26:05.720
Of course.

00:26:16.650 --> 00:26:19.090
Magnetic cushion flooding, drive away, generators off.

00:26:19.650 --> 00:26:21.310
Orion floods magnetic cushion.

00:26:24.030 --> 00:26:24.630
Distance 800.

00:26:25.070 --> 00:26:27.250
You can't go any lower, the FZ4 is too small.

00:26:27.780 --> 00:26:29.000
Relative speed 0.

00:26:30.030 --> 00:26:31.250
Why do we still have these three-person groups?

00:26:31.410 --> 00:26:33.330
That's why we're going to look into it now.

00:26:33.410 --> 00:26:34.670
I need two volunteers.

00:26:35.150 --> 00:26:38.250
Get used to looking for volunteers. No one goes voluntarily.

00:26:38.510 --> 00:26:40.130
Well, then you go, Hasso, and take...

00:26:40.130 --> 00:26:42.110
take Artan with you.

00:26:42.990 --> 00:26:44.390
Land Z1, destroy channel 1.

00:26:44.810 --> 00:26:46.740
And pull the pressure suits off.

00:26:46.740 --> 00:26:50.720
The oxygen system on MZ4 is as perfect as ours.

00:26:50.940 --> 00:26:53.540
Where a radio system is wrong, a oxygen system can also be wrong.

00:26:53.860 --> 00:26:54.960
Go, shut down the Land Z.

00:26:55.080 --> 00:26:57.890
Why are you doing this, Commander?

00:26:58.330 --> 00:26:59.780
Don't listen to him.

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:00.560
What are you doing in my place?

00:27:01.340 --> 00:27:02.560
I'm sticking to my orders.

00:27:02.760 --> 00:27:05.200
That's what a robot does.

00:27:05.280 --> 00:27:08.410
Since I've known you, I don't think robots are inferior anymore.

00:27:08.410 --> 00:27:09.570
They at least do their duty.

00:27:09.890 --> 00:27:11.590
Why do you need people then?

00:27:11.960 --> 00:27:13.060
You're not wrong about that.

00:27:13.100 --> 00:27:15.910
A robot would calculate much faster than any human being,

00:27:16.270 --> 00:27:17.370
which is not true down there.

00:27:54.000 --> 00:27:59.310
Course is programmed.

00:28:04.080 --> 00:28:05.380
Lanzet 1, please, top!

00:28:06.230 --> 00:28:15.390
Fuel, oxygen, radio, green, checked.

00:28:17.720 --> 00:28:18.340
Cliff, we're ready.

00:28:19.110 --> 00:28:19.830
Then nothing, out of the way!

00:28:20.930 --> 00:28:21.650
Attention, hazzard!

00:28:30.760 --> 00:28:31.220
Thank you.

00:29:09.600 --> 00:29:11.340
What do you think? Should we put the things on there?

00:29:11.420 --> 00:29:12.440
You heard it.

00:29:12.460 --> 00:29:15.920
Where a radio station is spinning, a oxygen station can spin, too.

00:29:58.540 --> 00:29:59.160
Just as little oxygen.

00:30:00.320 --> 00:30:01.460
Like in a deep-sea aquarium.

00:30:01.860 --> 00:30:05.640
The hydroponic system has to be destroyed.

00:30:06.210 --> 00:30:06.330
Yes.

00:30:30.830 --> 00:30:32.310
And the light distributors don't work either.

00:30:32.980 --> 00:30:33.300
Weird.

00:30:33.620 --> 00:30:36.030
Weird? I laughed more.

00:31:00.920 --> 00:31:01.180
Thank you.

00:32:12.540 --> 00:32:15.460
Look at this. The frequency controller is on a frequency that we never use.

00:32:17.960 --> 00:32:19.500
Somewhere the guys have to be stuck.

00:32:20.460 --> 00:32:21.000
Which guys?

00:32:22.080 --> 00:32:23.480
Clarence and his people. Who else?

00:32:23.720 --> 00:32:27.140
Exactly. Who else? I have the feeling that someone else is running around here.

00:32:54.670 --> 00:32:56.800
So, in motion, the fork in the hand.

00:33:31.480 --> 00:33:35.370
Do you think it has anything to do with the oxygen system?

00:33:36.240 --> 00:33:38.620
Nonsense. Looks like a human being has been stabbed.

00:33:39.230 --> 00:33:39.990
But what should...

00:35:00.090 --> 00:35:27.440
I'll go right away.

00:35:28.660 --> 00:35:29.720
Sipjon is on MZ-4.

00:35:30.060 --> 00:35:30.860
Call the Orion 7!

00:35:32.950 --> 00:35:34.090
Sipjorns on MZ-4, call!

00:35:34.210 --> 00:35:34.750
What's going on, Hasso?

00:35:35.640 --> 00:35:36.380
We're all dead.

00:35:37.300 --> 00:35:38.890
Clarence and the whole crew.

00:35:39.170 --> 00:35:39.760
Do you hear me?

00:35:39.980 --> 00:35:41.360
Yes, we understand you, Hasso.

00:35:41.380 --> 00:35:41.540
Go on.

00:35:41.820 --> 00:35:43.720
There must be extraterrestrials here.

00:35:44.860 --> 00:35:45.220
Extraterrestrial.

00:35:45.440 --> 00:35:48.390
What, here in this area?

00:35:48.450 --> 00:35:48.930
That's not possible.

00:35:49.090 --> 00:35:49.770
Cliff, it has to be.

00:35:50.030 --> 00:35:51.630
They're immune to our radiation weapons.

00:35:52.320 --> 00:35:52.840
Where are you?

00:35:52.920 --> 00:35:54.020
In Clarence's control room.

00:35:54.540 --> 00:35:54.880
Did you notice?

00:35:55.300 --> 00:35:55.580
Sure.

00:35:55.760 --> 00:35:58.670
I don't know why they haven't killed us long ago like Clarence.

00:35:59.170 --> 00:35:59.970
Do it as fast as you can.

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:01.760
Come back to the land as soon as possible! Go, you have to get out of here!

00:36:01.800 --> 00:36:03.600
It's okay, Cliff. We'll try.

00:36:05.760 --> 00:36:07.180
Prepare for alarm start, occupy combat position.

00:36:07.660 --> 00:36:08.420
Permanent surveillance of space.

00:36:09.710 --> 00:36:11.630
Extraterrestrial creatures in our galaxy?

00:36:12.050 --> 00:36:14.850
MZ-4 is one of the outermost bases on the edge of no man's space.

00:36:15.210 --> 00:36:17.120
Are there any signs that...

00:36:17.120 --> 00:36:19.620
For our century you have a richly anthropocentric world view.

00:36:20.040 --> 00:36:23.140
Alone in our Milky Way system there are four to ten billion planets

00:36:23.140 --> 00:36:24.840
on which intelligent life must be saved.

00:36:25.160 --> 00:36:27.880
Where do you take the arrogance to assume that we are the only ones

00:36:27.880 --> 00:36:28.560
who can multiply and multiply?

00:36:29.280 --> 00:36:29.940
I'm so stupid...

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:31.480
I don't think so either, but purely theoretically...

00:36:31.480 --> 00:36:33.160
What did Hasso just say? Did that sound theoretical?

00:36:34.310 --> 00:36:36.690
Orion 7 to engineer Sig Björnsson on MZ-4.

00:36:36.930 --> 00:36:38.470
Hasso, where are you now? Can you start?

00:36:38.890 --> 00:36:42.310
This is Sig Björnsson. Cliff, we're on our way to the landing shaft.

00:36:42.920 --> 00:36:44.580
Leave us alone. Do you have contact with him?

00:36:45.280 --> 00:36:49.510
No, leave us alone. I don't know why. We're moving on to the landing shaft.

00:36:50.140 --> 00:36:53.720
But if you've killed Clarence and his people, then why don't you attack Sig Björnsson and Shabashi?

00:36:54.000 --> 00:36:56.460
I can't think. I don't even read the alien ones.

00:36:56.520 --> 00:36:58.310
Cliff! Unknown flying objects!

00:36:58.670 --> 00:36:58.850
What?

00:36:59.170 --> 00:36:59.450
Here!

00:37:00.220 --> 00:37:00.700
Seven of them!

00:37:00.780 --> 00:37:01.940
Give me that!

00:37:09.060 --> 00:37:09.380
Distance?

00:37:10.000 --> 00:37:13.690
40, 9, 39, 8, 39, 6.

00:37:13.970 --> 00:37:14.660
My God, Cliff!

00:37:14.800 --> 00:37:16.280
You have insane speeds!

00:37:16.860 --> 00:37:18.000
We have to get out of here.

00:37:18.020 --> 00:37:19.280
We're sitting here like on the presentation plate.

00:37:19.480 --> 00:37:20.540
Ready for the alarm start.

00:37:20.780 --> 00:37:22.840
And what about Hasso and Artan?

00:37:23.000 --> 00:37:25.340
Where are the two of them?

00:37:26.100 --> 00:37:26.840
Hasso, Artan!

00:37:26.940 --> 00:37:27.560
What is it?

00:37:27.560 --> 00:37:28.400
Are you in the landing shaft?

00:37:28.500 --> 00:37:28.780
Why don't you start?

00:37:29.540 --> 00:37:29.980
We're in the...

00:37:33.320 --> 00:37:34.840
Damn it! You're under attack! Do you hear me, Hasso?

00:37:35.000 --> 00:37:37.380
Seven foreign objects! I can't wait any longer for you!

00:37:37.780 --> 00:37:39.540
Are you going to take me to a bomb shelter without me?

00:37:39.680 --> 00:37:41.460
I have to try! I have to go to the attack position!

00:37:42.060 --> 00:37:43.380
Get down there as fast as you can!

00:37:43.600 --> 00:37:45.000
We'll get you off behind here! End!

00:38:10.650 --> 00:38:12.360
Course balance, corrector programmed.

00:38:12.820 --> 00:38:14.460
Mario, we have to be at a distance in 130 seconds.

00:38:15.760 --> 00:38:16.820
I've got a job for you, too.

00:38:17.230 --> 00:38:19.230
Urgent message to ORB and TRAF.

00:38:19.370 --> 00:38:21.270
Exoteric on MZ-4, crew eliminated.

00:38:21.650 --> 00:38:23.190
Seven foreign aircraft on the approach.

00:38:23.490 --> 00:38:24.450
Combat operations ahead.

00:38:24.790 --> 00:38:25.480
Yes, but...

00:38:25.480 --> 00:38:26.460
What are you waiting for?

00:38:26.890 --> 00:38:29.390
I thought the entire radio traffic in this area was disturbed.

00:38:29.610 --> 00:38:29.690
Why?

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:33.500
Do what I tell you. We don't have time for explanations.

00:38:42.830 --> 00:38:49.580
Reflecting beam. Drawing objects. Twelve. Seven.

00:38:49.900 --> 00:38:51.480
What's taking so long?

00:38:51.820 --> 00:38:56.270
Five. Three. One. Zero.

00:38:57.430 --> 00:38:58.420
Free throw!

00:38:58.800 --> 00:38:59.740
That's a senseless clip.

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:01.080
They're way too far away!

00:39:01.380 --> 00:39:10.840
I think we'll attack them! They're invading the heavy field!

00:39:11.020 --> 00:39:12.490
Cliff! Our devices have fallen out!

00:39:12.990 --> 00:39:14.070
They've locked us in the heavy field!

00:39:14.590 --> 00:39:19.110
Throw them at us! Throw them at us!

00:39:19.210 --> 00:39:20.890
Get out of here, Cliff! For God's sake, get out!

00:39:20.950 --> 00:39:21.870
We've entered your heavy field!

00:39:22.370 --> 00:39:23.010
We're powerless!

00:39:23.690 --> 00:39:25.900
Switch to radio traffic!

00:39:26.280 --> 00:39:27.580
Get out of here, Major!

00:39:27.840 --> 00:39:29.760
You can't do it! Try to fall back!

00:39:30.860 --> 00:39:31.940
Retreat to MZ-4!

00:39:32.200 --> 00:39:35.570
Why MZ-4?

00:39:35.890 --> 00:39:37.560
I have to try to get them out of there!

00:39:37.580 --> 00:39:40.020
These brothers have a range we can't even dream of!

00:39:40.040 --> 00:39:42.040
That's hopeless, Major!

00:39:42.360 --> 00:39:44.040
They'll get us in and then...

00:39:44.040 --> 00:39:44.960
But I can't just let them rot!

00:39:45.580 --> 00:39:46.620
But it's more than that!

00:39:46.800 --> 00:39:50.800
The Orion has been disturbed by foreign objects in an inexplicable way!

00:39:51.000 --> 00:39:54.570
All data on this phenomenon is stored in the electron brain!

00:39:54.610 --> 00:39:56.330
This material has to go to Earth!

00:39:56.510 --> 00:39:57.550
This could be the beginning of an invasion!

00:39:58.920 --> 00:39:59.970
Cliff, we have to...

00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:03.120
They're a year ahead of us. When they get closer, they'll crush us like nothing.

00:40:03.730 --> 00:40:05.630
I think they don't want anything from us. I've calculated their course.

00:40:06.110 --> 00:40:07.090
They want to go to MZ-4.

00:40:07.470 --> 00:40:08.550
Yes, and we can't do anything.

00:40:08.990 --> 00:40:09.950
We have to do something.

00:40:10.330 --> 00:40:11.450
Oh yes, and what, please?

00:40:11.710 --> 00:40:16.800
You know the Alpha instruction 3B for all cruiser commanders just as well as I do.

00:40:17.710 --> 00:40:20.960
Commander, tell us the truth now.

00:40:21.020 --> 00:40:25.520
Do you technically have the possibility to eliminate the base MZ-4 before we're taken in?

00:40:25.840 --> 00:40:27.000
Technically, yes, by energy fire.

00:40:27.200 --> 00:40:29.960
But as long as the slightest possibility exists that Sigbjorns and Shubashins...

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:31.320
No human being can live without me!

00:40:31.320 --> 00:40:35.940
Every space base is in the event of a sudden attack by extraterrestrial forces or living beings,

00:40:36.100 --> 00:40:39.400
without considering their own losses, immediately eliminated.

00:40:39.940 --> 00:40:44.620
I give you Alpha Order to follow this order.

00:40:45.600 --> 00:40:47.280
You are a...

00:40:47.280 --> 00:40:49.300
She's right, Mario, she's right.

00:40:49.680 --> 00:40:58.350
Not a word about Trav.

00:40:58.370 --> 00:40:59.970
Major McLean...

00:41:00.000 --> 00:41:07.020
on the fast space cruiser Orion 7. Destroy the base of MZ-4 by energy fire on behalf of the security officer,

00:41:07.020 --> 00:41:11.980
because the base is safely in the hands of exotericists. Enemy objects are

00:41:11.980 --> 00:41:19.640
far above speed, so fall back to earth. Loss report. Engineer Hasso Sieg-Björnsen and

00:41:19.640 --> 00:41:27.220
Astrogator Artan Shubashi. End. Turn off the heaters. I wouldn't have dared to do that to you.

00:41:27.640 --> 00:41:29.980
You are no longer alive, or are you in the hands of the exotericists?

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:33.950
We have to try to reach them via radio.

00:41:34.810 --> 00:41:38.730
Should I call them and tell them, I'm sorry, but I'll kill you!

00:41:39.130 --> 00:41:41.850
Where do you want to go?

00:41:42.250 --> 00:41:43.500
Do you want to do it for me?

00:41:43.820 --> 00:41:46.930
Commander McKay!

00:41:46.930 --> 00:41:48.580
Commander, I'm begging for my service!

00:42:02.910 --> 00:42:04.930
Give it up. They've done a good job.

00:42:05.430 --> 00:42:08.240
You can say that. And we're in the trap.

00:42:08.460 --> 00:42:12.150
Cliff will get us out of here.

00:42:12.210 --> 00:42:14.800
If he can. If you ask me, man, it's over.

00:42:15.120 --> 00:42:16.340
But I won't ask you.

00:42:16.920 --> 00:42:19.690
If he got involved in a fight with the aliens, he's already dead.

00:42:19.910 --> 00:42:21.910
Did you forget that in there? The guy in the hallway?

00:42:22.350 --> 00:42:23.610
They're immune to our radiation.

00:42:24.170 --> 00:42:25.090
McLean doesn't stand a chance.

00:42:26.380 --> 00:42:27.140
We've often heard that.

00:42:37.930 --> 00:42:41.800
Mario, throw a two.

00:43:14.650 --> 00:43:16.590
Mr. McLane, you have to eliminate MZ-4!

00:43:17.430 --> 00:43:20.990
Yes, I have to. But I don't want to, do you understand?

00:43:21.250 --> 00:43:21.790
I can't!

00:43:22.110 --> 00:43:27.120
Cliff, they have blocked all our energy!

00:43:27.820 --> 00:43:29.240
What does that mean?

00:43:30.890 --> 00:43:31.910
I don't know either, but...

00:43:31.910 --> 00:43:34.540
We can't eliminate MZ-4 at all!

00:43:35.660 --> 00:43:48.880
Mifs, come closer! You have to speed up!

00:43:49.020 --> 00:43:54.540
We can't do anything here. So, speed up.

00:44:30.380 --> 00:44:31.780
Mr. Kleen can only destroy one of these things.

00:44:32.080 --> 00:44:36.100
So that means he's dead.

00:44:36.600 --> 00:44:37.460
Just like us.

00:44:37.620 --> 00:44:39.410
A few minutes.

00:44:40.100 --> 00:44:41.980
But a few of these Galat comrades too.

00:44:42.200 --> 00:44:43.260
What? Are you immune to fire weapons?

00:44:43.960 --> 00:44:46.480
They are the purest magic beings.

00:44:46.660 --> 00:44:47.910
You don't even need oxygen.

00:44:49.540 --> 00:44:53.700
We are idiots.

00:44:54.060 --> 00:44:57.600
They don't just need oxygen, they probably can't tolerate it at all.

00:44:57.600 --> 00:44:58.350
You think?

00:44:58.570 --> 00:44:58.770
Yes!

00:45:00.060 --> 00:45:01.080
find the hydrogen tank's circuit.

00:45:12.210 --> 00:45:13.010
What are you waiting for?

00:45:13.760 --> 00:45:14.640
They're taking the oxygen!

00:45:15.060 --> 00:45:17.130
And the others?

00:45:17.270 --> 00:45:18.550
The ones that land every moment?

00:45:19.050 --> 00:45:19.980
They won't get in

00:45:19.980 --> 00:45:21.460
if they notice that the oxygen is flooded.

00:45:21.920 --> 00:45:23.240
They have helmets against oxygen.

00:45:23.500 --> 00:45:25.220
Just like we have helmets for oxygen.

00:45:27.040 --> 00:45:27.980
We're going in and out.

00:45:28.720 --> 00:45:29.820
We'll explain it to his people.

00:45:30.000 --> 00:45:31.280
And why haven't you killed us long ago?

00:45:31.680 --> 00:45:33.440
What do I know? Maybe they want us alive.

00:45:33.820 --> 00:45:35.160
We're in a trap here.

00:45:35.820 --> 00:45:36.740
They're sure of their stuff.

00:45:37.020 --> 00:45:37.420
Why?

00:45:38.290 --> 00:45:40.010
They probably destroyed the oxygen system.

00:45:40.630 --> 00:45:41.490
But we'll see.

00:45:41.890 --> 00:45:43.110
I'm going to flood this room.

00:45:43.250 --> 00:45:59.540
So you're getting...

00:46:00.220 --> 00:46:00.800
We have to try.

00:46:01.140 --> 00:46:06.820
Too late! They're landing.

00:46:06.980 --> 00:46:24.060
Our Lancet.

00:46:24.350 --> 00:46:24.890
They're going into the tank.

00:46:26.300 --> 00:46:26.600
Starhouse.

00:46:26.720 --> 00:46:27.490
Do you want to get him?

00:46:28.240 --> 00:46:29.620
Of course we can kill ourselves right away.

00:46:32.360 --> 00:46:32.560
Thank you.

00:47:00.320 --> 00:47:00.600
Bye, Dad.

00:47:33.840 --> 00:47:34.260
Nothing but dust.

00:47:34.520 --> 00:47:36.170
What do you mean?

00:47:36.350 --> 00:47:46.680
This isn't oxygen for you.

00:47:46.680 --> 00:47:48.370
If this thing explodes...

00:47:48.370 --> 00:47:50.060
You think it's enough?

00:47:50.760 --> 00:47:53.000
What's enough for 90 days will probably be enough for this albino station.

00:47:53.480 --> 00:47:54.520
And I'll go with you then.

00:47:54.600 --> 00:47:56.190
All right, let's go.

00:48:21.370 --> 00:48:22.050
You don't have a helmet!

00:48:33.290 --> 00:48:34.560
I'm ready.

00:48:34.800 --> 00:48:36.430
Wait a minute.

00:48:37.270 --> 00:48:39.590
And what if the first ones are already here?

00:48:40.550 --> 00:48:41.570
Don't lose your nerve.

00:48:41.790 --> 00:48:43.460
We have to wait until the last one is in.

00:49:00.820 --> 00:49:01.780
Please.

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:04.830
Then you can probably tell me how we get out of here now.

00:50:08.340 --> 00:50:10.700
Gentlemen, I don't know if this is the time for fundamental discussions.

00:50:11.040 --> 00:50:14.540
The situation is that one of our advanced external bases is occupied by exotericists.

00:50:14.860 --> 00:50:20.400
So we are faced with the phenomenon that an extraterrestrial, space-driving race enters our highlands.

00:50:20.940 --> 00:50:22.000
It was to be expected sooner or later.

00:50:22.660 --> 00:50:24.420
Your leniency calms me down enormously.

00:50:24.880 --> 00:50:29.970
Did you perhaps also expect that these contemporaries against us...

00:50:30.000 --> 00:50:32.280
that they are immune to radiation weapons, and that they own spaceships,

00:50:32.640 --> 00:50:34.860
which, what was the name of the last report of McLean, General?

00:50:35.120 --> 00:50:39.530
If McLean is no other means than the escape, then that means that...

00:50:39.530 --> 00:50:42.660
I have moved the first and second strategic space fleet into alert condition

00:50:42.660 --> 00:50:44.640
and ask for release of the command.

00:50:45.140 --> 00:50:47.000
I don't know if this is the right measure.

00:50:47.580 --> 00:50:49.020
So, what should we do in your opinion?

00:50:49.400 --> 00:50:51.190
Wait until they occupy the other bases?

00:50:51.690 --> 00:50:54.490
I think it's too early to take strategic measures against an enemy

00:50:54.490 --> 00:50:57.330
from whom we don't even know exactly if it's your enemy at all.

00:50:57.330 --> 00:50:59.610
When the clock suddenly appears in front of our house door...

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:01.300
and immediately eliminated the crew of NZT.

00:51:01.760 --> 00:51:03.260
Do you think that's good manners?

00:51:03.660 --> 00:51:06.880
In a cosmos whose number of milky-street systems

00:51:06.880 --> 00:51:08.840
we can't even estimate closely,

00:51:09.490 --> 00:51:12.330
you wouldn't expect that our idea of good manners

00:51:12.330 --> 00:51:12.730
is in common.

00:51:13.330 --> 00:51:15.650
But we had no idea about you before.

00:51:15.650 --> 00:51:16.930
We've been receiving signals for centuries

00:51:16.930 --> 00:51:19.170
from all kinds of alien worlds that...

00:51:19.170 --> 00:51:21.210
I don't care about these alien worlds, as long as you leave us alone.

00:51:21.930 --> 00:51:25.430
I consider this attitude to be a bit antiquated.

00:51:25.430 --> 00:51:26.430
I have to beg you.

00:51:26.550 --> 00:51:27.670
It's really strange.

00:51:28.030 --> 00:51:29.830
With our Fortschütte we...

00:51:30.000 --> 00:51:31.260
the colonies on Mars and elsewhere.

00:51:31.880 --> 00:51:35.680
But the attitude of our generals has been the same for thousands of years.

00:51:35.980 --> 00:51:39.560
We are we, and if we act differently, then we take the light cannon.

00:51:39.960 --> 00:51:41.580
The question is whether we have another option.

00:51:42.910 --> 00:51:44.570
So, Willan, what do you advise?

00:51:44.770 --> 00:51:47.610
I warn against entering into larger combat actions

00:51:47.610 --> 00:51:48.450
before we know exactly.

00:51:49.010 --> 00:51:50.410
First, who are you?

00:51:50.750 --> 00:51:53.430
Second, what do you want? And third, what can you do?

00:51:53.470 --> 00:51:54.250
What you can do?

00:51:54.790 --> 00:51:57.050
That's what the McLane will sing a song about.

00:51:57.800 --> 00:51:59.320
Jupiter outer base reporting.

00:52:00.920 --> 00:52:03.050
Cliff, we'll be home soon.

00:52:03.110 --> 00:52:03.450
Yes.

00:52:04.660 --> 00:52:06.650
Light speech on Jupiter outside.

00:52:07.110 --> 00:52:09.090
Passing through Normala, ask for one-dive coordinates Terra.

00:52:09.270 --> 00:52:21.960
Amanda, I can imagine how you feel.

00:52:22.500 --> 00:52:27.000
I don't want to push myself, but if it relieves you,

00:52:27.360 --> 00:52:29.080
I'm ready to talk to Mrs. Sieg-Björnsen.

00:52:30.990 --> 00:52:33.780
Thank you, that's... I thank you, but I have to do it myself.

00:52:33.880 --> 00:52:37.220
After all, if it weren't for me, then Hasso would have long...

00:52:37.220 --> 00:52:40.730
Cliff! Cliff, we're idiots here, we forgot something.

00:52:40.910 --> 00:52:41.970
Yes, the Challenger, I know.

00:52:42.170 --> 00:52:45.790
Yes, if we don't do anything, the lab cruiser will crash into the MZ-4 in four hours, we have to redirect it!

00:52:46.490 --> 00:52:49.730
Why? The MZ-4 is in the hands of exotericists, Hasso and Arthan are dead.

00:52:49.950 --> 00:52:53.470
The lab cruiser is fully automatic, no one on board, only radioactive explosives.

00:52:54.130 --> 00:52:58.210
So the Challenger will do exactly what we couldn't do.

00:52:59.250 --> 00:52:59.870
MZ-4...

00:53:00.000 --> 00:53:00.540
Eliminate.

00:53:00.540 --> 00:53:18.880
Please, new coordinates.

00:53:19.710 --> 00:53:26.520
Distance 47, 7, 47, 6, 46, 500.

00:53:26.790 --> 00:53:29.480
Please, new coordinates.

00:53:30.730 --> 00:53:34.080
Critical distance. Critical distance.

00:53:34.840 --> 00:53:38.840
Challenger receives your critical distance.

00:53:39.260 --> 00:53:41.530
Accept new coordinates.

00:53:42.270 --> 00:53:43.970
This is to despair.

00:53:44.440 --> 00:53:46.620
We're done with everything. We're done with the exotericists.

00:53:47.180 --> 00:53:49.780
Now we're fed up with such an idiotic lab cross on our heads.

00:53:50.020 --> 00:53:53.290
If we receive the Challenger, then it must be just as possible

00:53:53.290 --> 00:53:55.410
that the Challenger receives our impulses.

00:53:55.710 --> 00:53:56.770
Understand, do you have it?

00:53:56.990 --> 00:53:59.630
They have the system for their frequencies.

00:54:00.000 --> 00:54:03.860
I'm not one of those frogs. I don't know how I can correct this crap.

00:54:04.910 --> 00:54:07.010
That's what the fleet's biggest astrogator is called.

00:54:07.370 --> 00:54:13.070
Challenger on exit 4. Critical distance. Critical distance.

00:54:13.740 --> 00:54:26.920
Requesting new coordination. Departure 36, 35, 35, 4, 34, 3, 33, 2.

00:54:27.760 --> 00:54:29.980
Challenger on exit...

00:54:30.160 --> 00:54:54.250
Who do you actually owe your rescue?

00:54:54.410 --> 00:54:57.850
I mean, who brought the Challenger to the explosion before it could crash onto MZ-4?

00:54:58.770 --> 00:54:59.960
That was...

00:55:00.000 --> 00:55:00.280
Who were the frogs?

00:55:01.050 --> 00:55:01.490
Frogs?

00:55:01.510 --> 00:55:01.690
Yes.

00:55:01.790 --> 00:55:02.840
The exotericists.

00:55:03.100 --> 00:55:06.120
We called them frogs, but that sounded too familiar, too earthly.

00:55:06.320 --> 00:55:07.270
That's why we called them frogs.

00:55:07.730 --> 00:55:11.080
I think the frogs were already killed by their oxygen reserves.

00:55:11.400 --> 00:55:11.760
That's right.

00:55:12.140 --> 00:55:16.320
Fortunately, they had a magnet shield built around the MZ-4, and then the Challenger

00:55:16.320 --> 00:55:16.620
was shattered.

00:55:16.960 --> 00:55:20.740
Only our Landsat let them through, because they obviously wanted us to be test rabbits.

00:55:21.380 --> 00:55:24.140
And then, of course, it was just a child's play to put the lighting system back

00:55:24.140 --> 00:55:25.560
in order and to call for help.

00:55:26.000 --> 00:55:26.620
Child's play?

00:55:26.960 --> 00:55:29.410
You took at least 17 hours for that.

00:55:30.160 --> 00:55:32.160
And? Time has no longer played a role.

00:55:32.640 --> 00:55:37.210
If you knew that the plan was to eliminate Mz.4

00:55:37.210 --> 00:55:38.630
through the second galactic fleet,

00:55:39.810 --> 00:55:41.050
you'd have been in for 17 hours.

00:55:42.210 --> 00:55:43.380
You want to chase us up?

00:55:45.350 --> 00:55:47.030
What would we have to thank you for?

00:55:47.250 --> 00:55:49.300
If you had time, you could thank someone.

00:55:50.420 --> 00:55:52.530
Besides, you were told that you were dead.

00:55:52.990 --> 00:55:56.580
But if you want to thank me, please do it with my boss.

00:55:57.000 --> 00:55:59.420
He has been prevented from taking measures against MZ-4.

00:56:00.000 --> 00:56:06.140
You have come surprisingly close.

00:56:06.640 --> 00:56:10.370
I think Lieutenant Jagilovsk will get used to us.

00:56:10.860 --> 00:56:12.900
Who gets used to whom, Major, will show the future.

00:56:13.480 --> 00:56:17.330
At least I will not get used to one thing for sure. That you lie to me.

00:56:17.450 --> 00:56:19.680
Did I lie to you?

00:56:19.820 --> 00:56:24.710
Of course. Or how was it with the pigeon nut that disturbs the radio traffic?

00:56:26.010 --> 00:56:27.410
That was ...

00:56:27.410 --> 00:56:29.160
That was a lie, Major.

00:56:30.120 --> 00:56:31.300
And if you think you can't...

00:56:31.300 --> 00:56:33.600
But, sir, those are problems you can solve with Commander McLane.

00:56:35.240 --> 00:56:37.120
If you were to drink one...

00:56:37.120 --> 00:56:38.540
Who says I never drink?

00:56:39.180 --> 00:56:40.890
You said it yourself on board.

00:56:41.250 --> 00:56:42.310
On board, Major?

00:56:42.830 --> 00:56:44.630
But who forces us to do our business?

00:56:45.000 --> 00:56:46.040
to discuss it on board.

00:56:46.360 --> 00:56:48.300
There's also a Starlight casino for that.

00:56:48.940 --> 00:56:50.020
Well, come on.

00:56:50.160 --> 00:56:53.020
I think you'll be allowed to go to a good party.

00:56:53.080 --> 00:56:56.360
But, man, this was probably just a bad dream.

00:56:56.520 --> 00:56:58.880
Much worse. It was science fiction.
